<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- The Argon2id password hashing surface targets all three LTS/STS lines.
         The PostQuantum.Jwt hybrid-token integration is net10.0-only because the
         BCL post-quantum primitives (ML-DSA/ML-KEM) and PostQuantum.Jwt itself
         ship for .NET 10. That code is gated behind #if NET10_0_OR_GREATER and a
         conditional package reference — see Tokens/ and KNOWN-GAPS.md. -->
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <RootNamespace>PostQuantum.Identity</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>PostQuantum.Identity</AssemblyName>
    <!-- The net10 token surface serializes claims via source-generated
         JsonTypeInfo<T> (PostQuantumIdentityJsonContext) and PostQuantum.Jwt's
         typed WithClaim<T> overload, so it is trim/AOT-clean. The Argon2id path
         (Konscious + Identity.Core) raises no trim warnings for our usage either.
         Asserted on net10 only — the trim/AOT analyzers ship with that SDK band. -->
    <IsAotCompatible Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">true</IsAotCompatible>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- NuGet package metadata -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>PostQuantum.Identity</PackageId>
    <Version>1.0.0</Version>
    <Title>PostQuantum.Identity — post-quantum ASP.NET Core Identity</Title>
    <Authors>Paul Clark</Authors>
    <Description>Post-quantum integration for ASP.NET Core Identity, with two surfaces at deliberately different scopes. (1) Argon2id password hashing for every deployment — PHC-formatted, secure-by-default work factors, transparent rehash-on-login, one-line PBKDF2→Argon2id migration via AddArgon2idPasswordHasherWithMigration, fail-closed verification with bounded parse cost, RFC 9106 §5.3 Known Answer Tests + reference-CLI PHC interop + emitter wire-format pin + deterministic generative fuzz corpus. Runs on net8.0 / net9.0 / net10.0. (2) Hybrid post-quantum JWT issuance for owned/trusted ecosystems (you control both the issuer and every verifier) — ML-DSA-65 signatures (FIPS 204) with optional X-Wing (X25519 + ML-KEM-768) encryption, kid-based key rotation, JSON-source-gen claim path, built on PostQuantum.Jwt 1.0.0 (stable). Uses non-IANA algorithm identifiers; intentionally not interoperable with generic JWT tooling until the IETF JOSE PQC drafts land. Requires .NET 10 (and OpenSSL 3.5+, 3.x series, on Linux). Supply chain: embedded CycloneDX SBOM, GitHub Sigstore-signed build-provenance attestation (verifiable with gh attestation verify), NuGet Trusted Publishing, deterministic SourceLink builds, .snupkg symbols, CodeQL, Dependabot. 1.0 is a semver API-stability commitment — NOT an audit claim; the library is not independently audited, stated plainly in SECURITY.md. See https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-identity for the full stance, migration guide, quantum-readiness playbook, and runnable issuer/verifier/key-tool samples.</Description>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-identity</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-identity</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageTags>aspnetcore;identity;aspnet-identity;password-hashing;argon2;argon2id;phc;owasp;jwt;jwt-token;post-quantum;pqc;quantum-resistant;ml-dsa;ml-kem;x-wing;hybrid-cryptography;authentication;cryptography;security;fips-204;sbom;cyclonedx;net8;net9;net10</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
1.0.0 — Stable API on stable upstream.

What 1.0 means: the public API only breaks with a major version (semver),
and the token surface now builds on PostQuantum.Jwt 1.0.0 STABLE (verified:
zero API drift, 442 tests green with zero skips on the PQ-capable lanes,
issuer/verifier samples exercised end-to-end).

What 1.0 does NOT mean: an audit (no third party has reviewed this library —
if your organization requires one, 1.0 does not change your answer), or
generic-JWT interoperability (alg = ML-DSA-65 stays deliberately non-IANA
until the IETF JOSE PQC drafts land; upstream adopts the standardized
identifiers then, picked up here via a normal version bump).

Everything below shipped the same day in the 0.6 line:

Security (one behavior change, in the fail-closed direction):
  - PHC verification acceptance bounds: a poisoned stored row can no longer
    demand an absurd Argon2id computation (m=2147483647 was a ~2 TiB
    allocation attempt per verify). Accepted: m in [8 KiB, 4 GiB],
    t in [1, 512], p in [1, 64] (m >= 8p), salt in [8, 64] B,
    tag in [12, 512] B. Out-of-range fails closed before any allocation.
  - Canonicality pins: exactly one accepted spelling per hash — canonical
    unpadded base64 for salt/tag (whitespace + trailing-bit aliases
    rejected), no leading-zero numeric aliases, and oversized fields
    rejected on length before any decode work.
  - Argon2idOptions.Validate() gains matching upper bounds so the emitter
    can never produce a hash its own verifier refuses.
  - BREAKING if you ever ran an out-of-range config (e.g.
    DegreeOfParallelism above 64): stored hashes from such configs no
    longer verify and there is no automatic recovery — read the CHANGELOG
    and docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md before upgrading.
  - New deterministic generative (fuzz-style) corpus for the PHC parser;
    acceptance bounds pinned at both edges of every axis.

Samples — the full provision → issue → verify → rotate lifecycle:
  - NEW Verifier.Demo: a separate resource service validating tokens across
    a real process boundary with only public keys (no Identity, no
    passwords, no private keys). The "you own both the issuer and every
    verifier" topology, runnable.
  - NEW KeyTool: generate/inspect ML-DSA-65 keys as (optionally encrypted)
    PKCS#8 + SPKI PEM. Pure BCL, zero dependencies.
  - Issuer demo can now load KeyTool-provisioned keys (PQ_ISSUER_KEY_DIR).
  - .http walkthrough files for all three web samples.

Docs: NEW docs/QUANTUM-READINESS.md (what to do about the quantum threat,
in what order) and docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md (symptom → cause → fix).

Infrastructure: NuGet Trusted Publishing (no long-lived API key),
Argon2id benchmarks in CI with a regression budget, macOS discovery lane.

NOT independently audited — every remaining gap is in KNOWN-GAPS.md.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <Copyright>Copyright © Paul Clark</Copyright>
    <NeutralLanguage>en-US</NeutralLanguage>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Symbols + SourceLink for debuggable, reproducible packages. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Argon2id implementation (Argon2 1.3 spec, PHC winner). Used on every TFM. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Konscious.Security.Cryptography.Argon2" Version="1.3.1" />
    <!-- Framework-agnostic ASP.NET Core Identity core: IPasswordHasher<TUser>,
         PasswordHasher<TUser>, IdentityBuilder, UserManager<TUser>. No EF / web host pulled in. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Identity.Core" Version="8.0.0" />
    <!-- For the opt-in AddPostQuantumPreflightLogging() hosted service. The
         abstractions package keeps the dep surface tiny — no full host runtime
         pulled in for callers who never opt in. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting.Abstractions" Version="10.0.11" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Hybrid-token integration: PostQuantum.Jwt + BCL PQC ship for .NET 10 only. -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="PostQuantum.Jwt" Version="1.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="../../LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Generate a CycloneDX SBOM (bom.json) inside the package on every Pack.
       Requires the `dotnet-CycloneDX` global tool (one-time install via
       `dotnet tool install` with the `global` flag and id `CycloneDX`). If the
       tool isn't present (e.g. a fresh dev machine), pack continues without the
       SBOM rather than failing; the release workflow installs the tool
       unconditionally, so CI always produces the SBOM.

       The bom.json is added via an in-target ItemGroup because
       $(IntermediateOutputPath)bom.json doesn't exist when a static <None Include>
       would be evaluated. Pinned to the net10.0 graph so the tool runs once. -->
  <Target Name="GenerateCycloneDxSbom"
          BeforeTargets="GenerateNuspec;_GetPackageFiles"
          Condition="'$(IsPackable)' != 'false' and '$(SbomDisabled)' != 'true'">
    <!-- IMPORTANT: the disable-package-restore flag is required. CycloneDX
         otherwise runs its own restore, and on a multi-targeted project that
         rewrites obj/project.assets.json to a single TFM, which then collapses
         the per-TFM dependency groups in the generated .nuspec (NU5128) and would
         drop transitive deps for net8.0/net9.0 consumers. With restore disabled
         it reads the existing multi-TFM assets and aggregates all frameworks. -->
    <Exec Command="dotnet CycloneDX &quot;$(MSBuildProjectFullPath)&quot; --disable-package-restore --output &quot;$(IntermediateOutputPath.TrimEnd('\').TrimEnd('/'))&quot; --filename bom.json --json"
          IgnoreExitCode="true"
          ContinueOnError="WarnAndContinue">
      <Output TaskParameter="ExitCode" PropertyName="_CycloneDxExitCode" />
    </Exec>
    <Message Importance="high"
             Text="CycloneDX SBOM not generated (tool missing or failed, exit=$(_CycloneDxExitCode)). Install with: `dotnet tool install` (global, id=CycloneDX)."
             Condition="'$(_CycloneDxExitCode)' != '0'" />
    <ItemGroup Condition="Exists('$(IntermediateOutputPath)bom.json')">
      <None Include="$(IntermediateOutputPath)bom.json" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <Message Importance="high"
             Text="CycloneDX SBOM packed into .nupkg at /bom.json"
             Condition="Exists('$(IntermediateOutputPath)bom.json')" />
  </Target>

</Project>
